cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or artifact, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "DATP-CP: Calibration-Channel Poisoning of Federated Threshold Personalization in IoT Anomaly Detection"
abstract: >
  Code and curated reproducibility artifacts for the DATP-CP study on
  calibration-channel poisoning in federated IoT anomaly detection. The artifact
  supports the N-BaIoT experiments with physical devices as clients and the
  GLOBAL_THRESHOLD, LOCAL_THRESHOLD, and CLUSTER_THRESHOLD policies. Training
  data, model weights, aggregation, test scores, and test labels remain clean.
